From 9e3697f3ede0d83b8adfa7911a2815d2e290f019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Flatt <oflatt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 01:10:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shrink_slots: use the orbit-closed slot set it already
 computes

Shrinking a class whose group is non-trivial panics:

    term  (f (var $0) (var $1))
    union (f (var $0) (var $1)) (f (var $1) (var $0))
    union (f (var $0) (var $1)) (g (var $1) (var $1))

    SlotMap::index($f2): index missing!   (group/mod.rs, build_ot)

restrict_proven filters a permutation by its *keys*, so with cap = {1} the swap
{0->1, 1->0} becomes {1->0}, which maps a surviving slot outside cap. That is not a
permutation of cap, and composing it later indexes a slot the map does not have.

final_cap is exactly the guard against this -- it removes the orbit of every newly
redundant slot, so no surviving slot can be moved out -- but it was computed and then
discarded, with c.slots and the generator restriction both taking cap. Using it fixes
the panic. In the case above orbit(0) = {0,1}, so final_cap is empty and both slots are
correctly redundant, which is what the comment on the loop already says.

Neither half alone reproduces: the symmetry union and the shrinking union are both
needed.

No test changes: 105 pass before and after, with the same three pre-existing
redundancy_matching_bug failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/egraph/rebuild.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/egraph/rebuild.rs b/src/egraph/rebuild.rs
index 425543f..b8e4142 100644
--- a/src/egraph/rebuild.rs
+++ b/src/egraph/rebuild.rs
@@ -91,6 +91,7 @@ impl<L: Language, N: Analysis<L>> EGraph<L, N> {
             final_cap = &final_cap - &grp.orbit(d);
         }
 
+        let cap = final_cap;
         c.slots = cap.clone();
         let generators = c.group.generators();
         let _ = c;
